# ProfileInfoListResponse, hand-built rather than captured: this project's
# own test eUICC has no profiles installed at all (omnikey-profiles.log,
# a real capture, answers with an empty profileInfoListOk) -- so there is
# no real card to capture actual ProfileInfo content from. The SELECT
# ISD-R exchange here is the same real-hardware bytes every other
# recording in this directory uses (this card's own FCI); only the
# STORE DATA response for BF2D00 is synthetic, produced by the generated
# der_encode, not hand-invented -- see this directory's README.md for the
# throwaway program and how to reproduce this exact payload.
#
# Two ProfileInfo entries: the first carries every field
# rsp_card_read_profiles reports (iccid, isdpAid, profileState,
# profileNickname, serviceProviderName, profileName, profileClass); the
# second carries only iccid and profileState, exercising the fact that
# every other one of those fields is genuinely OPTIONAL in rsp-2.5.asn
# and a real card is free to omit any of them.
